<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Markdown on the parser</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="@spell-app/markdown:  GitHub-flavoured markdown on the generic parser, drawing ui-* elements;  how it's built, where it plugs in, and its numbers."
    />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../../tools/_assets/spell-doc.css" />
  </head>
  <body class="spell-doc-page">
    <spell-site-header root="../../../.."></spell-site-header>
    <div class="spell-doc">
      <main class="spell-doc-main">
        <ui-breadcrumb class="spell-crumbs" size="small" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <ui-breadcrumb-section href="../index.html" target="src-packages-docs-index-html">Docs</ui-breadcrumb-section>
          <ui-breadcrumb-section active>Markdown on the parser</ui-breadcrumb-section>
        </ui-breadcrumb>
        <ui-sticky class="spell-h1"
          ><header class="spell-page-head"><h1>Markdown on the parser</h1></header></ui-sticky
        >
        <p class="lede">
          <code>@spell-app/markdown</code> (<code>MD</code>): GitHub-flavoured markdown on the generic parser, the
          second language on it after spell. How it's built, where it plugs in, and what it costs.
        </p>
        <ui-list class="spell-meta">
          <ui-item icon="user"
            >Written for: anyone changing
            <a href="../../../markdown/" target="src-packages-markdown"><code>packages/markdown</code></a
            >, or deciding whether it replaces marked</ui-item
          >
          <ui-item icon="flag"
            >Status: <ui-label size="mini" color="green">built</ui-label> (branch <code>markdown</code>)</ui-item
          >
          <ui-item icon="flask"
            >Checked on: branch <code>markdown</code>, 2026-10-04, with the GFM spec suite and the experiments in
            <a href="#5-sources">Sources</a></ui-item
          >
          <ui-item icon="map"
            >Plan doc:
            <a href="../epics/markdown/markdown.plan.html" target="markdown">epics/markdown/markdown.plan.html</a>; the
            rulex changes it drove:
            <a href="../rulex/rulex.html" target="src-packages-docs-content-rulex-rulex-html">rulex</a></ui-item
          >
        </ui-list>

        <ui-section id="1-summary" header="1. Summary" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
          <ui-icon slot="icon" name="lightbulb"></ui-icon>
          <ui-statistics class="spell-stats" size="mini">
            <ui-statistic value="670/670" label="GFM spec examples"></ui-statistic>
            <ui-statistic value="1.8×" label="marked's time"></ui-statistic>
            <ui-statistic value="59 kB" label="bundle, gzipped"></ui-statistic>
          </ui-statistics>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Markdown in, <code>P.Markup</code> out, as plain HTML or with <code>ui-*</code> elements (<code
                >MD.render(text, { ui: true })</code
              >).
            </li>
            <li>
              Passes every GFM spec example (670/670), with GitHub's extensions on: tables, task lists, strikethrough,
              autolinks, the tag filter, and alerts (<code>&gt; [!NOTE]</code>).
            </li>
            <li>
              Line kinds are rulex rules; the container stack and the inline pass (emphasis, links) are hand-written
              ports of commonmark.js 0.29. Rulex can't say "the open containers" or "pair these delimiters".
            </li>
            <li>
              1.8× marked's time over the repo's 172 <code>.md</code> files (101 ms vs 56 ms); 2.2 ms for the biggest
              (32 kB). Fast enough to re-render on every keystroke.
            </li>
            <li>
              Too big to replace marked everywhere yet: the browser bundle is 59 kB gzipped (88 kB before its
              bundle-time cuts) vs marked's 14 kB, DOMPurify now loading only for <code>sanitized</code>. So plain
              <code>&lt;ui-markdown&gt;</code> keeps marked, and only <code>&lt;ui-markdown editable&gt;</code> loads
              <code>MD</code>.
            </li>
            <li>
              In use: the app's docstrings (<code>&lt;Markdown&gt;</code>), the LSP's colouring of markdown in comments,
              and <code>&lt;ui-markdown editable&gt;</code>'s preview.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <ui-message state="info" header="Next">
            <ul>
              <li>
                Slim the bundle (HTML entities, lodash,
                <a href="../../../parser/src/ast/AST.ts" target="src-packages-parser-src-ast-ast-ts"
                  ><code>AST.ts</code></a
                >: plan doc I6), then swap plain <code>&lt;ui-markdown&gt;</code> over.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </ui-message>
        </ui-section>

        <ui-section id="2-the-package" header="2. The package" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
          <ui-icon slot="icon" name="layer group"></ui-icon>
          <p>
            <a href="../../../markdown/" target="src-packages-markdown"><code>packages/markdown</code></a> depends only
            on <code>$/parser</code> and <code>$/util</code>. Its shape follows commonmark: blocks first, then inlines
            inside each leaf block.
          </p>

          <ui-section id="how-it-flows" header="How it flows" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <ui-steps class="spell-steps" ordered>
              <ui-step
                header="normalize"
                description="Line endings to \n, NUL to U+FFFD (markdown.types.ts)."
              ></ui-step>
              <ui-step
                header="blocks"
                description="BlockScanner reads line by line:  container prefixes, then one rulex line rule per kind;  out comes a Block tree whose leaves hold raw text."
              ></ui-step>
              <ui-step
                header="references"
                description="extractReferences() pulls link reference definitions out of paragraphs:  document-global, so before any inline."
              ></ui-step>
              <ui-step
                header="inlines"
                description="InlineParser turns each leaf's text into InlineNodes (with source positions):  code spans, links, emphasis by delimiter stack;  then GFM autolinks."
              ></ui-step>
              <ui-step
                header="render"
                description="renderBlocks / renderInlines build P.Markup (plain or ui-*);  markupToHTML() writes it."
              ></ui-step>
            </ui-steps>
          </ui-section>

          <ui-section id="the-parts" header="The parts" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <ui-cards class="spell-flow" stackable>
              <ui-card>
                <ui-content>
                  <ui-header>MarkdownTokenizer</ui-header>
                  <ui-description
                    >Words, one symbol per other character, whitespace riding on the token before it, so rulex's spacing
                    sees it.</ui-description
                  >
                </ui-content>
              </ui-card>
              <ui-card>
                <ui-content>
                  <ui-header>lineRules</ui-header>
                  <ui-description
                    >8 line kinds in rulex: thematic break, ATX heading, fence, setext underline, list markers, table
                    delimiter row ...</ui-description
                  >
                </ui-content>
              </ui-card>
              <ui-card>
                <ui-content>
                  <ui-header>BlockScanner</ui-header>
                  <ui-description
                    >The open-container stack, lazy continuation, list tightness, GFM tables. A port of commonmark.js
                    0.29's blocks.</ui-description
                  >
                </ui-content>
              </ui-card>
              <ui-card>
                <ui-content>
                  <ui-header>InlineParser</ui-header>
                  <ui-description
                    >Delimiter and bracket stacks, references, entities, raw HTML. A port of commonmark.js 0.29's
                    inlines.</ui-description
                  >
                </ui-content>
              </ui-card>
              <ui-card>
                <ui-content>
                  <ui-header>render</ui-header>
                  <ui-description
                    >Block and inline trees to <code>P.Markup</code>; GitHub heading slugs, the
                    <code>ui-*</code> mapping, alerts, tasks.</ui-description
                  >
                </ui-content>
              </ui-card>
            </ui-cards>
          </ui-section>

          <ui-section id="rulex-vs-code" header="Rulex vs hand-written" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Rulex says what a line IS: each line kind is a rule, asked with
                <code>lineRules.matchWhole(tokens, "atx_heading")</code>.
                <ul>
                  <li>
                    The scanner reads columns, levels and info strings from the raw text: they're about characters, not
                    tokens.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    Cheap one-character guards (<code>LINE_GUARDS</code>, a regex per kind) skip a rule that can't
                    match: they took the block phase from 342 ms to 50 ms over the repo's files.
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li>
                Hand-written: the container stack (block quotes and list items nest, and continue lazily) and emphasis
                (<code>*</code> / <code>_</code> runs pair by the left- / right-flanking rules). Neither is a grammar a
                rule can say.
              </li>
              <li>The inline pass is a straight port, not rulex: most of it is "any token but X" scanning.</li>
            </ul>
            <ui-accordion class="spell-code" styled>
              <ui-title>packages/markdown/src/blocks/lineRules.ts (excerpt) · 14 lines</ui-title>
              <ui-content>
                <pre><code class="language-ts">/** Three or more of one of `-`, `*`, `_`, spaced or not. */
class thematic_break extends P.Sequence {}
lineRules.addRule(thematic_break, { syntax: "(- {3,}|\\* {3,}|_ {3,})" })

/** A run of 1-6 `#`, then nothing, or a space and anything. */
class atx_heading extends P.Sequence {}
lineRules.addRule(atx_heading, { syntax: "#{1,6}" })
lineRules.addRule(atx_heading, { syntax: "#{1,6}{spaces}{any}*" })

/** A run of 3+ backticks or tildes, then any info string. */
class fence_open extends P.Sequence {}
lineRules.addRule(fence_open, { syntax: "(`{3,}|~{3,})" })
lineRules.addRule(fence_open, { syntax: "(`{3,}|~{3,}) {any}+" })</code></pre>
              </ui-content>
            </ui-accordion>
          </ui-section>

          <ui-section id="the-api" header="The API" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <ul>
              <li><code>MD.toHTML(text, options)</code>: plain HTML, as the spec writes it.</li>
              <li><code>MD.toMarkup(text, options)</code>: the <code>P.Markup</code> tree.</li>
              <li>
                <code>MD.render(text, options)</code>: <code>{ markup, html, headings }</code>, with <code>ui</code>,
                <code>headingIds</code> (GitHub's slugs), <code>headingOffset</code>, <code>breaks</code>,
                <code>autolinks</code> and <code>tagfilter</code>.
              </li>
              <li>
                Raw HTML passes through; the caller sanitizes (<code>&lt;ui-markdown&gt;</code> uses DOMPurify unless
                <code>trusted</code>).
              </li>
            </ul>
          </ui-section>
        </ui-section>

        <ui-section id="3-where-it-plugs-in" header="3. Where it plugs in" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
          <ui-icon slot="icon" name="code branch"></ui-icon>

          <ui-section id="ui-mapping" header="The ui-* mapping" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <ui-table celled compact striped unstackable>
              <table>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <th>markdown</th>
                    <th>plain</th>
                    <th><code>ui: true</code></th>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>heading</td>
                    <td><code>&lt;h1 id&gt;</code></td>
                    <td><code>&lt;ui-header level id&gt;</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>list</td>
                    <td><code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;ol&gt;</code></td>
                    <td>
                      <code>&lt;ui-list bulleted | ordered&gt;</code>, numbered by <code>value</code>; tasks only: no
                      bullets; bullets inside a numbered list stay <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>task item</td>
                    <td><code>&lt;input type=checkbox disabled&gt;</code></td>
                    <td><code>&lt;ui-checkbox readonly&gt;</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>alert (<code>&gt; [!NOTE]</code>)</td>
                    <td><code>&lt;blockquote&gt;</code></td>
                    <td><code>&lt;ui-message state icon header&gt;</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>quote</td>
                    <td><code>&lt;blockquote&gt;</code></td>
                    <td><code>&lt;ui-segment secondary&gt;</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>table</td>
                    <td><code>&lt;table&gt;</code></td>
                    <td><code>&lt;ui-table celled&gt;&lt;table&gt;</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>code block</td>
                    <td><code>&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;</code></td>
                    <td><code>&lt;ui-code language copy&gt;</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>---</code></td>
                    <td><code>&lt;hr&gt;</code></td>
                    <td><code>&lt;ui-divider&gt;</code></td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </ui-table>
          </ui-section>

          <ui-section id="app-docstrings" header="App docstrings" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <a href="../../../app/src/solid/Markdown.tsx" target="src-packages-app-src-solid-markdown-tsx"
                  ><code>packages/app/src/solid/Markdown.tsx</code></a
                >
                draws docstrings with <code>MD</code> (marked is gone from <code>app</code>).
              </li>
              <li>
                It imports <code>$/markdown</code> LAZILY (an async memo + <code>&lt;Loading&gt;</code>, plain text
                meanwhile): the runner and <code>&lt;spell-app&gt;</code> show docstrings too, and a static import would
                put the parser in every runner bundle.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </ui-section>

          <ui-section id="lsp-colouring" header="LSP colouring" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <code>SpellLanguageService</code>'s semantic tokens colour markdown inside comments: four new modifiers,
                <code>bold</code>, <code>italic</code>, <code>link</code> and <code>strikethrough</code>, from
                <code>MD</code>'s inline source positions.
              </li>
              <li>
                Every comment, not only docstrings: telling them apart needs the parse, and spell's comments are
                markdown-styled anyway.
              </li>
              <li>
                The VS Code extension declares and styles the modifiers; it needs <code>yarn vscode</code> from
                <code>main</code> after the merge (a worktree build would bake in the worktree's path).
              </li>
              <li>Checks in docstrings (broken <code>#heading</code> links, unknown identifiers): a todo.</li>
            </ul>
          </ui-section>

          <ui-section id="ui-markdown-editable" header="<ui-markdown editable>" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <code>ui</code> never imports <code>$/markdown</code>'s source: <code>yarn gen:markdown</code> (in
                <a href="../../../ui/" target="src-packages-ui"><code>packages/ui</code></a
                >) bundles it into
                <a
                  href="../../../ui/src/components/ui-markdown/md.bundle.js"
                  target="src-packages-ui-src-components-ui-markdown-md-bundle-js"
                  ><code>src/components/ui-markdown/md.bundle.js</code></a
                >, as <code>gen:spell</code> does spell's highlighter.
              </li>
              <li>
                <code>editable</code> adds Write / Preview tabs. The preview loads <code>MDEngine</code> (its own lazy
                chunk) and draws with <code>ui-*</code> elements, sanitized by DOMPurify with <code>ui-*</code> tags
                allowed.
              </li>
              <li>
                Each preview renders the whole text (~2 ms), then swaps only the top-level blocks whose markup changed,
                so unchanged code blocks aren't re-highlighted. No incremental parser: it would buy ~2 ms for a lot of
                complexity (lazy continuation, document-global references).
              </li>
              <li>Plain <code>&lt;ui-markdown&gt;</code> still uses marked: see the bundle size below.</li>
            </ul>
          </ui-section>
        </ui-section>

        <ui-section id="4-numbers" header="4. Numbers" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
          <ui-icon slot="icon" name="bullseye"></ui-icon>

          <ui-section id="spec" header="GFM spec" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <ul>
              <li>
                All 670 examples of cmark-gfm's <code>spec.txt</code> pass, vendored as
                <code>src/spec/gfm-spec.json</code> (<code>yarn spec:update &lt;spec.txt&gt;</code>).
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="../../../markdown/src/spec/spec.test.ts" target="src-packages-markdown-src-spec-spec-test-ts"
                  ><code>spec.test.ts</code></a
                >
                pins the pass count per section in a snapshot: a regression fails, a gain updates it. The tag filter and
                extended autolinks are per-example options, as the spec tests them.
              </li>
              <li>
                <code>yarn tsx scripts/spec-report.mts [section…]</code> (in
                <a href="../../../markdown/" target="src-packages-markdown"><code>packages/markdown</code></a
                >) prints the failures of a section.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </ui-section>

          <ui-section id="vs-marked" header="Against marked" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <ui-table celled compact striped unstackable>
              <table>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <th>over the repo's 172 .md files (1315 kB)</th>
                    <th class="num right aligned">MD</th>
                    <th class="num right aligned">marked 18</th>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>time, median of 7</td>
                    <td class="num right aligned">101 ms</td>
                    <td class="num right aligned">56 ms</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>same HTML (normalized)</td>
                    <td class="num right aligned" colspan="2">156 of 172</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>browser bundle, gzipped</td>
                    <td class="num right aligned">59.4 kB</td>
                    <td class="num right aligned">14.2 kB</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </ui-table>
            <ul>
              <li>The 16 files that differ are spec-conformance cases: MD follows the spec where marked doesn't.</li>
              <li>
                Of MD's 101 ms, the block phase is 50 ms: it was 342 ms before the line guards (<a
                  href="experiments/profile.mts"
                  target="src-packages-docs-content-markdown-experiments-profile-mts"
                  ><code>profile.mts</code></a
                >
                has the rest).
              </li>
              <li>
                One file: 2.2 ms for
                <a href="../../../spell/PARSING.md" target="src-packages-spell-parsing-md"
                  ><code>packages/spell/PARSING.md</code></a
                >
                (32 kB).
              </li>
            </ul>
          </ui-section>

          <ui-section id="bundle" header="The bundle" sticky collapsible dividing collapsed>
            <p>
              <a
                href="../../../ui/src/components/ui-markdown/md.bundle.js"
                target="src-packages-ui-src-components-ui-markdown-md-bundle-js"
                ><code>md.bundle.js</code></a
              >
              is 257 kB raw. Where the bytes go:
            </p>
            <ui-table celled compact striped unstackable>
              <table>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <th>module</th>
                    <th class="num right aligned">kB raw</th>
                    <th>slimming</th>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>entities</code> (HTML5 entity table)</td>
                    <td class="num right aligned">52.2</td>
                    <td>decode through the browser</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>lodash (through <code>$/util</code>'s barrel)</td>
                    <td class="num right aligned">43.1</td>
                    <td><code>$/util</code>'s generic files only</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      the parser's
                      <a href="../../../parser/src/ast/AST.ts" target="src-packages-parser-src-ast-ast-ts"
                        ><code>AST.ts</code></a
                      >
                    </td>
                    <td class="num right aligned">31.0</td>
                    <td>out of the parser barrel</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      <a href="../../../parser/src/rulex/rulex.ts" target="src-packages-parser-src-rulex-rulex-ts"
                        ><code>rulex.ts</code></a
                      >, Tokenizer
                    </td>
                    <td class="num right aligned">22.3</td>
                    <td>needed</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>BlockScanner, InlineParser</td>
                    <td class="num right aligned">18.1</td>
                    <td>needed</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>pluralize, chalk</td>
                    <td class="num right aligned">11.2</td>
                    <td>with lodash</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </ui-table>
          </ui-section>
        </ui-section>

